From: pas7std co-op <coop@pas7std.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0009/0009] native NPC store: stop re-cloning and re-stringifying the whole root on every read

A live V8 CPU profile of the running server (1 ms sampling, 17 453 samples over
20 s, ~100 NPCs) attributed 62.7% of self time to cloneValue and 24.0% to
ensureRootShape in server/src/space/npc/nativeNpcStore.js. Every readCollection,
writeCollectionRow and removeCollectionRow re-read the entire NPC root (entities,
modules, cargo, wrecks for every system), deep-cloned it twice through
JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) and compared two full JSON.stringify results.

Rows are only ever written through subpaths (`/<collection>/<rowID>`), so the
default root keys cannot disappear after the first verification. The root shape is
now verified once per table per process, and readCollection reads only the
collection it was asked for.

No game rule changes: same data, same shape, same write paths. Measured on the
same server afterwards: cloneValue fell from 86.7% to 41.9% of samples and the
process went from 0% idle to 32.7% idle.
